      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, are we handling the [third corner case](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AsWN58i1Tk4eut1qkTn1Jns9aJQX73fXogHvbXbFVxs/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-JQTku6jCH4gGgBq8eyzdbA\u0026tab\u003dt.0#heading\u003dh.mxmx6vwogv1w) through these changes as well? Since the suppression logic is currently wrapped inside the `if (chipset_in_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ON) \u0026\u0026 tablet_get_mode())` check, I was wondering how the code handles a situation where the OS successfully enters suspend (S3) while the user is still holding the button. The expected behavior is that if the user accidentally presses and holds the power button just before the OS enters suspend, the release of the power button should be ignored so it doesn\u0027t wake up the OS again.",
